    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "textbook-why-ignore",
        "moduleId": "why-ignore",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "教材：并非每个文件都需要历史",
        "markdown": "教材开篇指出：我们并不总是希望 Git 记录每个文件的历史。例如，可能希望跟踪以 `.txt` 结尾的文本文件，但不跟踪以 `.dat` 结尾的数据文件。如果不做处理，每次调用 `git status` 时，Git 都会把这些文件列出来提醒我们。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-dacd3293b5aedfe0e5a195bd",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000026"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Using Git at the Command Line",
                "Ignoring Files"
              ],
              "lineStart": 2604,
              "lineEnd": 2633,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "5546e859ee44f44101ea5865bcc160f49f4a50884abbab160e841cdc53f990bf"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-ignore-meaning",
        "moduleId": "why-ignore",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "补充：「忽略」作用在版本控制这一层",
        "markdown": "「忽略」针对的是版本控制的选择，不是文件本身：被忽略的文件仍然留在工作目录里，程序照常读写，只是 Git 不再提示它，也不会把它纳入提交。把这一区别记住，就能理解为什么忽略规则属于仓库配置，而不是数据清理手段。\n\n判断标准可以概括成一句话：这个文件能不能由仓库里的其他内容重新生成？能，就适合忽略。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-why-ignore"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-gitignore-rules",
        "moduleId": "ignore-rules",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "procedure",
        "title": "教材：创建并填写 .gitignore",
        "markdown": "教材给出的做法是：在项目根目录创建一个名为 `.gitignore` 的文件。文件里可以写具体文件名，例如 `thesis.pdf`，也可以写通配符模式，例如 `*.dat`。每条规则必须单独占一行，Git 会忽略匹配到其中任何一行的内容。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "paraphrase",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-dacd3293b5aedfe0e5a195bd",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000026"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Using Git at the Command Line",
                "Ignoring Files"
              ],
              "lineStart": 2604,
              "lineEnd": 2633,
              "assetRefs": [],
              "excerptSha256": "5546e859ee44f44101ea5865bcc160f49f4a50884abbab160e841cdc53f990bf"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "model-rule-anatomy",
        "moduleId": "ignore-rules",
        "depth": "support",
        "kind": "explanation",
        "title": "补充：一条规则怎么读",
        "markdown": "把一条规则读成「一个模式占一行」：\n\n- 一行只写一个模式，不要用逗号、空格或分号把多个模式挤在同一行；\n- `*.dat` 是通配符写法，概括所有以 `.dat` 结尾的文件；\n- 需要排除某个具体文件时，直接写出文件名，例如 `thesis.pdf`。\n\n若项目要跟踪文本文件、忽略数据文件，`.gitignore` 可以写成：\n\n```text\n*.dat\n```\n\n这只有一行，却覆盖了所有 `.dat` 文件；以后再新增同类数据文件，也不必回头改规则。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "model",
          "basedOnBlockIds": [
            "textbook-gitignore-rules"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "textbook-pycache-entry",
        "moduleId": "regenerable-boundary",
        "depth": "core",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "教材示例：只忽略 __pycache__",
        "markdown": "教材的示例项目在 `.gitignore` 里只写了一条：\n\n```text\n__pycache__\n```\n\n它让 Git 忽略 Python 生成的 `__pycache__` 目录。这类目录由 Python 自动产生，不是手写的源码。",
        "provenance": {
          "origin": "textbook",
          "representation": "quote",
          "sourceSpans": [
            {
              "materialId": "doc-dacd3293b5aedfe0e5a195bd",
              "blockIds": [
                "block-000026"
              ],
              "headingPath": [
                "Using Git at the Command Line",
                "Ignoring Files"
              ],
              "lineStart": 2604,
              "lineEnd": 2633,
              "assetRefs": [],
